Design choices: Complete, self-contained TSX module with balanced JSX, closed expressions, and a named GeneratedShot export. · Headline and kicker remain locked at their specified screen positions, outside the stage camera. · Camera follows the requested zoom and pan beats without overshoot. A per-frame bounds clamp trims the initial vertical offset enough to keep the amber strip below y1000. · Equal-height pillars, no axes or measurements, persistent blue traces, and retained panels communicate transaction history rather than quantitative comparison. · The return traversal is synchronized to verifiable; the emerald check appears only inside TX-A's reference panel after the cursor arrives. · Midnight gradients, a structural grid, blue directional light, rounded glass, colored shadows, and film grain provide the required five-layer finish. · The record ID is stable and can be supplied through recordId to preserve an upstream token; REC-01 is the standalone fallback.

